  "definition": "Stroke is a group of conditions in which neurological function is suddenly lost without convulsions because part of the brain is damaged by reduced blood flow or bleeding inside the skull. It can be described in different ways, including where the damage occurs, which blood vessels are involved, and whether bleeding is present.",
